  "answer": "# Final Comparison Report: Median Household Income (Indiana vs. United States)\n\n## Source Justification\nThe **Current Population Survey (CPS)** conducted by the U.S. Census Bureau was used for income data because it is the official government source for annual median household income estimates. The **Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (CPI-U)** from the Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS) was used for inflation adjustment as it is the standard official price index for measuring the purchasing power of urban households.\n\n## Income Data (2015-2023)\nThe following table presents the nominal and real median household incomes. Real income is expressed in 2023 dollars.\n\n| Year | US Nominal Income | IN Nominal Income | US Real Income (2023$) | IN Real Income (2023$) | Source(s) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 2015 | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | - |\n| 2016 | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | - |\n| 2017 | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | - |\n| 2018 | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | - |\n| 2019 | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | - |\n| 2020 | $68,010 [S25] | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | [S25] |\n| 2021 | $70,780 [S25] | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | [S25] |\n| 2022 | $74,580 [S25] | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | [S25] |\n| 2023 | $80,610 [S25], [S30] | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | BLOCKED | [S25], [S30] |\n\n## Percentage Change (Real Income 2015-2023)\n- **United States:** BLOCKED\n- **Indiana:** BLOCKED\n\n## Deliverables\n- **CSV File:** BLOCKED (Not generated in Step 8 due to missing input data).\n- **PNG Bar Chart:** BLOCKED (Not generated in Step 4 due to missing input data).\n\n## Limitations\nThe final report is significantly incomplete due to the following failures in the data pipeline:\n- **Step 1, 2, and 7 (Researcher):** Failed to retrieve nominal median household income for Indiana (2015-2023), US nominal income (2015-2019), and the official BLS CPI-U annual average index values (2015-2023).\n- **Step 3 and 8 (Analyst):** Unable to calculate real incomes or percentage changes because the necessary nominal and inflation data were BLOCKED.\n- **Step 4 (Visualization):** Unable to produce the PNG chart because the real income dataset was not available.\n- **Step 8 (Analyst):** Unable to produce the CSV file because the real income dataset was not available.\n\n- Mislabelled citation: step 1 cites S5 for '2016', which S5 does not contain; it is in S14 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 1 cites S5 for '2017', which S5 does not contain; it is in S14 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 1 cites S5 for '2018', which S5 does not contain; it is in S1, S14 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 1 cites S5 for '2019', which S5 does not contain; it is in S14 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 1 cites S5 for '2020', which S5 does not contain; it is in S7, S14 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 2 cites S5 for '2016', which S5 does not contain; it is in S12, S14, S19 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 2 cites S5 for '2017', which S5 does not contain; it is in S12, S14, S19 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 2 cites S5 for '2018', which S5 does not contain; it is in S1, S12, S14 (added by plain code)\n- Mislabelled citation: step 2 cites S5 for '2019', which S5 does not contain; it is in S12, S14, S23 (added by plain code)\n",
